# A Solid node can be used to represent objects in the simulated environment (e.g. obstacles, walls, ground, robot parts, etc.).
# Solid nodes can be collision detected (boundingObject) and therefore can prevent objects from intersecting.
# In addition, Solid nodes can have an optional Physics node that allow them to be simulated with the physics engine.
# parent: Pose

Solid {
  #fields that inherit from the Pose node:
  w3dField SFVec3f    translation         0 0 0
  w3dField SFRotation rotation            0 0 1 0
  w3dField MFNode     children            []           # shape and solids fixed to that solid
  #fields specific to the Solid node:
  w3dField SFString   name                "solid"      # used by wb_robot_get_device()
  field    SFString   model               ""           # generic name of the solid (eg: "chair")
  field    SFString   description         ""           # a short (1 line) of description of the solid
  field    SFString   contactMaterial     "default"    # see ContactProperties node
  field    SFString{"ode", "newton", "auto"} physicsBackend "auto"  # "auto" (default) resolves to Newton, the only backend. "newton" pins it explicitly. ⚠ "ode" is a RETIRED SELECTOR, not a fallback: ODE was deleted, so a Solid pinned to it is not simulated AT ALL (no contact, no gravity) and the engine warns once. It is kept because worlds in the wild contain it, and because it is used deliberately as a "do not simulate this" switch for hologram / ghost robots.
  field    SFNode     boundingObject      NULL         # for collision detection
  field    SFNode     physics             NULL         # optional Physics node
  field    SFBool     locked              FALSE        # to avoid moving objects with the mouse
  # Whether the CLOTH solver can see this body. Only read on the coupled path (WorldInfo.newtonSolver "mujoco+vbd"); inert everywhere else, including "vbd", where one solver owns everything by construction and there is no proxy roster to narrow.
  #   0  (default) = unset. Leave every Solid at 0 and the world behaves EXACTLY as it did before this field existed: every rigid body is a cloth proxy.
  #   1            = couple. Declaring 1 on ANY Solid switches the world to ALLOWLIST mode -- from then on ONLY the Solids declaring 1 are visible to the fabric.
  #  -1            = do not couple. Subtractive; use it to drop a few bodies without listing every one you want to keep.
  # WHY YOU WANT THIS. newton clears COLLIDE_SHAPES|COLLIDE_PARTICLES on every shape whose body is not a proxy (solver_coupled.py:805-838), so the roster is the cloth's whole collision world. Left at the default, that is EVERY body in the scene -- every table, wall and arm link broadphased against the sheet every step. newton's own Franka cable demo lists just the hand and fingers. For a gripper closing on fabric the answer is usually two pads.
  # ⚠ THE TRAP, AND IT FAILS SILENTLY: a body left OFF the roster is invisible to the cloth and the fabric falls straight THROUGH it. Only world/static shapes (newton's body -1, i.e. the implicit z=0 ground plane) survive narrowing -- an authored floor or table Solid is a real body and must be named to be seen. Narrow the roster and the engine logs the resolved list; read it. Resolving to zero bodies falls back to all of them with a warning rather than shipping a cloth that collides with nothing.
  # The narrowing touches only the cloth's view: it is written through a copy-on-write shape_flags array, so MuJoCo's own rigid-rigid contact is unaffected no matter what is declared here. OMNISIM_CLOTH_COUPLED_BODIES overrides ("all", or a comma-separated newton body-index list).
  field    SFInt32    newtonClothCoupling 0            # -1 / 0 / 1: hide from / leave to the runtime / show to the cloth solver
  field    SFFloat    radarCrossSection   0.0          # radar cross section of this solid
  field    MFColor    recognitionColors   []           # colors returned for this Solid by Cameras with a Recognition node
  #fields that inherit from the Pose node:
  field    SFFloat    translationStep     0.01         # step size used by translation manipulator
  field    SFFloat    rotationStep        0.261799387  # step size used by rotation manipulator (PI/12)
  # hidden fields
  hiddenField SFVec3f linearVelocity      0 0 0        # (m/s) Solid's initial linear velocity
  hiddenField SFVec3f angularVelocity     0 0 0        # (rad/s) Solid's initial angular velocity
}
